<title>USA: N.J. Supreme Court upholds pension bond deal.</title>
<headline>N.J. Supreme Court upholds pension bond deal.</headline>
<dateline>TRENTON, N.J. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Jersey Democrats have lost their last chance to undo the state's $2.8 billion pension bond issue, after the state Supreme Court turned down an appeal on Monday.</p>
<p>The bonds also formally changed hands on Monday, with buyers of the issue getting their certificates and the state getting its money.</p>
<p>The bond issue was key to Gov. Christine Whitman's budget plans for the fiscal year that began at midnight, and freed up about $590 million in one-shot savings.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
